      "source": [
        "##In this project, I work with the MNIST dataset to explore how unsupervised learning can be applied to image data. I begin by loading and preprocessing the dataset directly through Scikit learn, normalizing the images and flattening them for analysis. After a brief exploratory data review, I apply K Means clustering to identify natural groupings in the data and use the elbow method to estimate the optimal number of clusters. I then evaluate the model by assigning cluster labels to new images and checking how well these assignments fit the learned structure. Finally, I use PCA and t SNE to reduce the dimensionality of the dataset and visualize the clusters in two dimensions, allowing me to assess the effectiveness of the clustering process and better understand the relationships between different groups."
      ],
